as many of you know intel the company  that for many years enjoyed a monopoly  over the cpu industry  isn't doing so well anymore consumers  who once defended intel with all of  their might on various internet forums  have slowly faded away and the worst  part is that the future for intel  is starting to look incredibly grim but  to be honest this shouldn't surprise  anybody we've known that intel was in  trouble for years now  in fact back in 2019 almost a full year  before  apple officially announced their  transition from intel  chips we made this video and the funny  thing about the thumbnail  is that it's actually starting to become  reality in that video  we made a couple of predictions on how  intel would eventually end up  fighting for the life of their business  and so far  half of it has already come true so let  me quickly go over some key points in  that video before i get into how bad of  a situation  intel is in today and to make things  interesting  i'm gonna be referring to the five  stages of grief  to chart where intel is at at each point  in the story  so let's get right into it in the early  2000s and 2010s  intel enjoyed the bulk of the cpu market  share  especially for gaming so they got a bit  cocky in 2013  and announced a very optimistic cpu  roadmap  promising that they'd be shipping  nanometer chips  in 2015. to do that they were gonna use  a brand new chip making technology  against the wishes of some of their  engineers and it ended up getting  delayed over and over and over again  all the way out to 2019 by the way intel  was in the first stage of grief during  that time  denial now while that was happening amd  came out of the shadows with their  impressive ryzen  and threadripper cpus which caused some  serious pain to intel  and we know this because intel started  lowering the prices of their chips  to compete with amd on top of that  within just a couple of years  intel very quickly upped the core count  on their desktop trips  from 4 cores all the way up to 10  trying to keep up with amd all while  using the same  old 14 nanometer chip architecture this  actually caused a lot of pain for apple  because the company literally redesigned  their 2016  super thin and light macbook pro with  intel's  10 nanometer chips in mind which were  supposed to be ready  by 2015 but they weren't and because of  that major delay  apple's macbook pros started having  major overheating issues  and apple took the blame for all of the  disappointment by their consumers  but thankfully in june of 2020  apple made perhaps the best decision  they could have  ever made they announced the switch away  from intel  over to their own apple silicon chips  essentially the same chips that come  in an ipad or an iphone just  souped up for high performance and now  we know  just how good of a decision that was by  apple  because intel's brand new 11th gen  desktop cpus are still being  built on a 14 nanometer process  which is just shameful at this point and  by the way  11 days before apple announced the  transition  intel's lead chip architect resigned  showing that they knew this was coming  and at this point in the story  they were well into the anger stage of  their grief  and then of course later in 2020 apple  revealed  their new m1 chip and ever since then  it's been an absolute slaughter fest for  intel  with the m1 max completely embarrassing  every intel base mac machine  out there in terms of performance power  usage and value  and based on the incredible sales data  for apple's new m1 max  it looks like consumers are all for  ditching intel  for apple's new custom chips oh and by  the way  intel got rid of their ceo bob swann  earlier this year more anger and now  here we are in april of 2021  and intel is doing things that we never  thought they'd do in a million years  they actually stole the mac guy from  apple's most famous ad  campaign and turned him against the mac  showing that he's now beginning to  prefer windows based laptops instead  this is perhaps the biggest act of  desperation  that intel has ever displayed once again  more anger but here's the thing about  intel's  new ad campaign that many people don't  realize  intel doesn't actually make windows  based laptops  they simply make chips for any platform  that wants some so they made an ad  campaign  against apple products even though they  don't make  any hardware products of their own to be  honest it should have been  microsoft the creators of windows who  ran  this ad campaign and not intel which is  ironic  so intel is basically sucking up to  microsoft  and windows based laptop makers which  shows how  desperately intel wants to keep their  business  just look at this image telling you to  quote go  pc but wait it gets even worse  and this is where the bargaining stage  of grief comes in  just days after their anti-apple ad  campaign launched  intel ceo mentioned that they want to  manufacture  apple silicon chips in the future yes  they actually had the guts  to say this in public after that ad  campaign which shows  just how desperate they are now why in  the world would they want to do this  well for security if their own x86 chips  start to lose market share at least  they'll be able to survive  by producing the very chips that led to  their demise  but in my opinion i don't think there's  any way that intel is getting apple's  business  ever again and here's why apple got  burned  many times by intel in the past from the  whole 10 nanometer chip delay  causing them embarrassment due to  overheating macbooks  to the various intel security flaws that  apple had to take the heat for  i don't think that apple wants to play  with fire again  and by the way apple has already  reserved years worth of chip orders with  tsmc  the most advanced chipmaker in the world  which seems to be the most resilient  to the global chip shortage that we're  currently going through  and since apple is tsmc's number one  customer  they will do everything possible to keep  up with the chip demand  specifically for apple so there's really  no point for apple to go with intel  especially since they're behind in terms  of chip making technology  so yeah intel is desperate and the worst  part of all  is that apple is just getting started  yes the m1 max are killing it  but it's the m1x macbook pros which are  gonna revolutionize the entire industry  and finally put the last nail in intel's  coffin  and put them into the next stage of  grief depression  so let's get into why the future looks  so grim for intel  right now in 2021 laptop manufacturers  have already started to offer  amd cpu models alongside intel versions  of their laptops  so intel is already losing market share  on that front  but on the other side apple's m1 max are  so impressive  that some laptop makers are reportedly  looking forward  to arm-based chips instead of x86  but they haven't seen nothing yet based  on our own estimates  the m1x macbook pros coming sometime  this fall  should be able to easily outperform  every single intel based macbook  at a fraction of the price but the most  important detail to consider  is that the power efficiency of these  macbooks  should be incredible thanks to how  efficient apple's arm-based chips have  proved to be  so there's a very good chance that the  m1x macbooks  will literally be the best laptops ever  made  and sooner or later the entire laptop  industry  will begin moving over to using  arm-based chips  and right now both samsung and qualcomm  are quietly sitting in the shadows with  their arm chips  waiting for this to happen and even  worse the folks over at microsoft the  makers of windows  have already announced that they're  going to be making arm-based chips of  their own  and going even further they've been  focusing more and more on updating  their arm-based version of windows ever  since  apple announced their transition this is  very bad  news for intel because if microsoft  makes the switch to arm based chips  it's going to show where the entire  industry is moving  since microsoft will be incentivized to  make the armed version of windows  the best that it can be to compete with  apple  so if the entire industry begins  transitioning to arm-based ships  then intel is basically screwed because  they're 13 generation raptor lake chips  coming in 2022 seem to still be using  the same x86 10 nanometer process as the  12th gen  alder lake which by the way isn't even  here yet  this puts intel in the worst possible  position because it's clear  that they're still not working on  arm-based designs  if they were they would have already  announced it in an attempt to make their  investors happy  but they didn't and by far the worst  thing is that their main competitor amd  is reported to be already working on  some arm-based chips of their own  to battle apple's m chips so when intel  does  eventually announce that they're working  on arm chip designs  it's probably going to be too late now i  know that some of you are going to say  that apple was only a small part of  intel's business  so it's not really going to matter sales  wise but one thing  is very clear the user sentiment towards  intel  has been rapidly changing to the  negative side  and that is more important than anything  else and just in case you're gonna say  that the book of intel's business  is actually the server or workstation  market  i've got some more bad news for you the  fastest servers in the world  are already using arm-based designs and  intel's future xeon road map  is purely x86 based and here is where  the other side of the danger lies  companies who host massive servers  require  many computers which causes a couple of  problems that need to be dealt with  first there's a huge amount of power  that's required to run the computers  and second there's the huge amount of  heat that the computers  output so they need massive cooling  systems  in order to keep them cool which also  use  tons of power we already showed this off  when we compared the performance per  watt  of apple's m1 mac mini to the  intel-based mac  pro the difference is massive so if  arm-based chips require  less power and less cooling while still  having awesome performance  why wouldn't the server or workstation  industry  move over to arm they're going to save  massive amounts of cash  just in electricity and cooling expenses  alone  scaleway is already offering cloud  services  using apple m1 mac minis for only 12  cents an hour  compared to amazon's web services which  use intel mac minis  for over a dollar an hour and people are  already surprised by the price  and it's all due to the power savings of  the m1 chip  oh and by the way amazon has already  announced that they're going to have  m1 mac minis available soon as well  so it looks like the server industry is  already  slowly beginning to switch to arm so to  sum up this entire video  apple basically triggered the death of  intel  with their apple silicon transition and  at this point  it's looking like intel's only way out  will be to start work on arm-based  designs  as soon as possible but at this point  they haven't been so i guess we'll just  have to wait and see  what the future holds for intel  hopefully you guys enjoyed this video  and if you learned something new go  ahead and click the circle above to  subscribe for more videos like this one  definitely check out one of those two  videos including the last version of  this video that we made  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video
 

